{
  "id": "poiseuille_s_formula",
  "title": "Poiseuille's Formula",
  "description": "Calculate the volume flow discharged through a smooth-walled circular pipe using Poiseuille's formula.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Poiseuille's Formula\n\nCalculate the volume flow discharged through a smooth-walled circular pipe.\n\n### Formula\n\n**V = π × p × r⁴ / (8 × η × l)**\n\nWhere:\n- **V** = discharge volume flow (m³/s)\n- **p** = pressure difference between the ends of the pipe (N/m², Pa)\n- **r** = internal radius of pipe (m)\n- **l** = length of pipe (m)\n- **η** = dynamic viscosity of fluid (Pa·s)"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "pressure_difference",
          "label": "Pressure Difference (p)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "defaultValue": 1000
        },
        {
          "id": "pipe_radius",
          "label": "Internal Radius of Pipe (r)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m",
          "defaultValue": 0.01
        },
        {
          "id": "pipe_length",
          "label": "Length of Pipe (l)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m",
          "defaultValue": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "dynamic_viscosity",
          "label": "Dynamic Viscosity (η)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "Pa·s",
          "defaultValue": 0.001
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "volume_flow",
          "label": "Discharge Volume Flow (V)",
          "formula": "3.14159 * inputs.pressure_difference * Math.pow(inputs.pipe_radius, 4) / (8 * inputs.dynamic_viscosity * inputs.pipe_length)",
          "unit": "m³/s",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}